tory."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final bout of the Games saw the emergence of a boxer who would become one of the professional side of the sport’s biggest stars in years to come. A late call up to the US team after the withdrawal of Buster Mathis, " [:a {:href "/athletes/8671"} "Joe Frazier"] " demolished his first three opponents before grinding out a points victory over " [:a {:href ""} "Hans Huber"] " of Germany to become heavyweight champion at Tokyo."] "\n\n" [:p {} "As ever there were many disputed decisions but this time protests got much uglier than usual. Spanish featherweight " [:a {:href "/athletes/2863"} "Valentin Loren"] " vented his frustrations at being disqualified by landing a punch on referee and promptly received a life ban from the sport. The next day " [:a {:href "/athletes/3324"} "José Roberto Chirino"] " of Argentina did exactly the same to earn a disqualification from his light-middleweight quarter-final. By contrast Korean " [:a {:href ""} "Jo Dong-Gi"] " opted for a more pacifist approach and protested his loss by sitting down in his corner and refusing to leave. His protest lasted 51 minutes."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/23312"} "Flyweight (≤51 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 – 23 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/23345"} "Bantamweight (≤54 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 – 23 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/23382"} "Featherweight (≤57 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "13 – 23 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a 